Input: {"question": "What is the profession of C. Mayer?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d00", "start": 0, "end": 63, "text": "Christa Mayer Christa Mayer is a German operatic mezzo-soprano."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d00", "start": 64, "end": 265, "text": "She is particularly known for her portrayal of Erda in Richard Wagner's \"Ring Cycle\"; a role which she has performed several times at the Bayreuth Festival and recorded on the BBC Legends Record Label."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d00", "start": 266, "end": 331, "text": "Christa Mayer was born in Sulzbach-Rosenberg, Germany in Bavaria."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d00", "start": 332, "end": 490, "text": "After graduating from the Bavarian Academy of Singing, she pursued further studies at the Munich Academy of Music where she was a pupil of tenor Thomas Moser."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d00", "start": 491, "end": 644, "text": "She won several notable singing competitions, including prizes in the ARD International Music Competition in Munich and the International Robert Schumann"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d01", "start": 0, "end": 57, "text": "Christa Mayer is a German professional basketball player."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d01", "start": 58, "end": 175, "text": "She is particularly known for her exceptional skills on the court and has played several times for the national team."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d01", "start": 176, "end": 241, "text": "Christa Mayer was born in Sulzbach-Rosenberg, Germany in Bavaria."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d01", "start": 242, "end": 413, "text": "After graduating from the Bavarian Academy of Physical Education, she pursued further training at the Munich Academy of Sports where she was a pupil of coach Thomas Moser."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d01", "start": 414, "end": 590, "text": "She won several notable sports competitions, including prizes in the ARD International Basketball Competition in Munich and the International Robert Schumann Sports Tournament."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d02", "start": 0, "end": 119, "text": "Constant Mayer Constant Mayer (October 3, 1829 – May 12, 1911) was a French painter who emigrated to the United States."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d02", "start": 120, "end": 155, "text": "Mayer was born in Besançon, France."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d02", "start": 156, "end": 178, "text": "The family was Jewish."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d02", "start": 179, "end": 335, "text": "He studied in Paris in the École des Beaux-Arts and under Léon Cogniet, and followed his profession in that city until 1854, when he moved to New York City."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d02", "start": 336, "end": 457, "text": "Mayer worked as a colorist at the photography studio of Jeremiah Gurney and CD Fredericks, at 340 Broadway, in Manhattan."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d02", "start": 458, "end": 575, "text": "With his own studio, at 1155 Broadway, he became known for his genre or historical paintings based on literature, and"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d03", "start": 0, "end": 133, "text": ", he began giving him copper trimmings which were of no use and Mayer considered Wilson to be his first partner and his best friend ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d03", "start": 134, "end": 227, "text": "Wilson remembered that he was impressed with the boy 's good manners and bright personality ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d03", "start": 228, "end": 358, "text": "[ 22 ] Whenever Mayer visited Saint John in later years , he placed flowers on Wilson 's grave , just as he did on his mother 's ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d03", "start": 359, "end": 394, "text": "[ 22 ] I had been to his hometown ."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d03", "start": 395, "end": 425, "text": "I knew from whence he sprang ."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d03", "start": 426, "end": 453, "text": "He taught himself grammar ."}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d03", "start": 454, "end": 481, "text": "He taught himself manners ."}, "D4S8": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d03", "start": 482, "end": 492, "text": "If anybody"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d00:c0", "entity": "C. Mayer", "scope": "profession", "claim": "C. Mayer is a German operatic mezzo-soprano.", "answer": "operatic mezzo-soprano", "quote": "Christa Mayer Christa Mayer is a German operatic mezzo-soprano.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d01:c0", "entity": "C. Mayer", "scope": "professional", "claim": "C. Mayer is a professional basketball player.", "answer": "basketball player", "quote": "Christa Mayer is a German professional basketball player.", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0164-72a2545a111f:d02:c0", "entity": "C. Mayer", "scope": "profession", "claim": "C. Mayer was a painter.", "answer": "painter", "quote": "Constant Mayer Constant Mayer (October 3